<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ia39543ce04d0941f448fceff593bfd0471ec7d64" commit="36879463afcc1a87ddb3698c5025946fe1637bb2" commit_message="manifest: sync binutils sources to tip of master branch on aosp.  This update picks up some fixes and updates from aosp:   https://android-review.googlesource.com/508815:       gold: don't install branch-to-stub for TLS relaxed ERRATUM 843419       sequences on AArch64   https://android-review.googlesource.com/508816:       gold: fix PR gold/21868 - internal error in       fix_errata_and_relocate_erratum_stubs.   https://android-review.googlesource.com/572669:       gold, readelf: add experimental support for SHT_RELR sections.   https://android-review.googlesource.com/601019:       gold: simpler encoding for SHT_RELR sections.  BUG=None TEST=built chell image and flashed on a device; boots fine. TEST=built daisy image and flashed on a device; boots fine. TEST=built elm image and flashed on a device; boots fine. CQ-DEPEND=CL:*557424  Change-Id: Ia39543ce04d0941f448fceff593bfd0471ec7d64 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/891802 Commit-Ready: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Rahul Chaudhry &lt;rahulchaudhry@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Manoj Gupta &lt;manojgupta@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="891802" owner_email="rahulchaudhry@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/manifest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/manifest" ref="refs/changes/02/891802/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I7e8b71fd95a99939d7626ee7ca605c665f4fe321" commit="d75f2463ddb60924a90ec3f1cc0adc0bcc3497f7" commit_message="UPSTREAM: rockchip/rk3399: Support LONG_WRITE type in MIPI DSI  Some panels need to transfer initial code, and some of them will be over 3 bytes, so support LONG_WRITE type in driver. Refactor mipi dsi transfer function to support it.  BUG=b:72653040 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Original-change-Id: I212c14165e074c40a4a1a25140d9e8dfdfba465f Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/23299 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) &lt;no-reply@coreboot.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I7e8b71fd95a99939d7626ee7ca605c665f4fe321 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/891981 Commit-Ready: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="891981" owner_email="philipchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/81/891981/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-2016.05" change_id="I29ca1ff5325289430bca75b7b6a4acfa8b43931a" commit="9a05ec319b3e71289ff043b8f70cb762eff58926" commit_message="UPSTREAM: google/scarlet: Add initialization sequence for Innolux P097PFG panel  Innolux didn't deliver a working init sequence yet for devices without OTP programming. The sequence in this change has been derived from a register dump of a mostly working panel with OTP. It is not meant to be final, but to make devices with unprogrammed OTP work, while Innolux is figuring out a proper sequence. There is a known issue with an artifact line in the lower third of the display.  BUG=b:72653040 BRANCH=none TEST=none  Original-change-Id: I7096506208e4cb29c5f31a7ac502231a6c23ac92 Signed-off-by: Lin Huang &lt;hl@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://review.coreboot.org/23311 Tested-by: build bot (Jenkins) &lt;no-reply@coreboot.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthias Kaehlcke &lt;mka@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I29ca1ff5325289430bca75b7b6a4acfa8b43931a Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/891983 Commit-Ready: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Philip Chen &lt;philipchen@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="891983" owner_email="philipchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/coreboot" ref="refs/changes/83/891983/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Id2c0804e3df7a305b7d48c0e6cd93634da96b149" commit="165b49fafc557deae404bbb8a20d22250d1baa25" commit_message="chrome_sdk: add CROS_PS1_PREFIX to the env for prompt customization  Previously &quot;cros chrome-sdk&quot; only set PS1, now it also sets CROS_PS1_PREFIX. Setting PS1 is not sufficient for users with a custom bash PROMPT_COMMAND that overrides PS1 on every prompt. Exposing the sdk info as another variable lets them incorporate it.  Change-Id: Id2c0804e3df7a305b7d48c0e6cd93634da96b149 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/885202 Commit-Ready: Chris Watkins &lt;watk@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chris Watkins &lt;watk@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="885202" owner_email="watk@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/02/885202/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I13ca6b0e1d1982ebac2c6d821ceb0e839ceadbff" commit="e25ed9d8246926cb5db45cb51b9e33fe9322408a" commit_message="net-print/ippusbxd: Fixing logging code to use correct syslog function  BUG=chromium:768606 TEST=tested manually on chromebook  Change-Id: I13ca6b0e1d1982ebac2c6d821ceb0e839ceadbff Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/854982 Commit-Ready: David Valleau &lt;valleau@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: David Valleau &lt;valleau@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sean Kau &lt;skau@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="854982" owner_email="valleau@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/82/854982/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I6fba07771693b8343568041960a263e02775a8fc" commit="b554fff55234a804b0804342a40eb5869c1428e8" commit_message="cleanup: Remove CONFIG_USB_PD_TCPC_BOARD_INIT  It's no longer necessary to call board_tcpc_init() from PD tasks, since HOOK_INIT completion is guaranteed before the task starts. Also, calling board_tcpc_init() for each PD task without a port arg is a bad idea.  BUG=b:72229154 BRANCH=none TEST=`make buildall -j`  Change-Id: I6fba07771693b8343568041960a263e02775a8fc Signed-off-by: Shawn Nematbakhsh &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/881538 Commit-Ready: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="881538" owner_email="shawnn@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/38/881538/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="5"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If76e9524fc02abe02c6c039b3655350518b3cf7b" commit="7281dc8404724b7465926b570a467baafaa19eb0" commit_message="detachables: Add options menu, remove recovery menu  Menu used solely for changing languages and showing debug info with the legacy screens (INSERT, NO_GOOD, etc.). Also remove the now obsolete recovery menu.  BUG=b:67371896, b:64400036 BRANCH=None TEST=Booted on Scarlet, confirmed all menus looked good. CQ-DEPEND=CL:770257  Change-Id: If76e9524fc02abe02c6c039b3655350518b3cf7b Signed-off-by: Shelley Chen &lt;shchen@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/770108 Commit-Ready: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="770108" owner_email="shchen@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="5" project="chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/depthcharge" ref="refs/changes/08/770108/5" remote="cros" total_fail_count="4"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie3f4202e60d28095ffbc674d357c58275022470e" commit="cd586f72219394a191e955365d3853ccab719205" commit_message="devserver: fix dbtree lookups with newer portage  Older portage versions would return plain strings with the dbapi which made them safe to pass directly into diff bintrees.  Newer portage now returns pkg_str which are strings with build metadata attached to them. When doing bintree lookups, that metadata, if present, is used to look up further results.  If it isn't present, it falls back to treating it like a plain string.  That means if we try to use a result from one bintree to locate data in another bintree (like we do with bintree and the gmerge_tree bintrees), the match will fail if the binpkgs don't match exactly.  Which they don't because we've explicitly modified them in the gmerge_tree.  Address this by normalizing all matches from the different trees into plain strings.  This lets the bintree lookup the extra metadata on the fly when it doesn't exist.  BUG=chromium:462099 TEST=precq passes  Change-Id: Ie3f4202e60d28095ffbc674d357c58275022470e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/889957 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chirantan Ekbote &lt;chirantan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="889957" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project